<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Magnis</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Kenchester</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Magnis was a small walled Roman town at Kenchester, west of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hereford">Hereford</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a>, on the road along the Welsh border. Excavations have traced its defences and buildings of the 2nd to 4th centuries. Its name may lie behind that of the Magonsaete, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anglo-saxons">Anglo-Saxon</a> people of the region.</p></div>
